<title>USA: International Aluminum Q2 shr eases.</title>
<headline>International Aluminum Q2 shr eases.</headline>
<dateline>MONTEREY PARK, Calif. 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter Ended December 31:	    1996		 1995</p>
<p> Sales				     $56,161,000    $54,354,000</p>
<p> Net income		     (a)	1,273,000	2,017,000</p>
<p> Earnings Per Share	   (a)		.30		.47</p>
<p>Average Shares outstanding</p>
<p>						 4,262,348	4,257,564</p>
<p>    Six Months Ended December 31:	 1996		 1995</p>
<p> Sales				     113,089,000    110,392,000</p>
<p> Net Income				  2,609,000	4,093,000</p>
<p> Earnings Per Share	   (a)		.61		.96</p>
<p>Average Shares outstanding</p>
<p>						 4,261,419	4,255,882</p>
<p>(a) Includes $508,000 or $.12 per share of restructuring and asset write- downs related to the purchase of Altura and subsequent merger into Raco in the quarter and $1,056,000 or $.25 per share in the six months related to restructuring charges and write-down of assets. SOURCE  International Aluminum Corporation</p>
</text>
